{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>וַיִּמָּלֵא שִׁבְעַת יָמִים.</b> Meaning, the limited measure set for the plague was completed, and after seven days were completed following the smiting, etc., then HaShem spoke. And the intent of the verse in this notification is that Pharaoh was not moved by this plague to ask Moses to pray to HaShem, and the plague remained until its limit — and this is what it says, <b>וַיִּמָּלֵא</b> etc., after HaShem had smitten, and the days of the plague were completed and fulfilled. Now, according to our Rabbis of blessed memory (Shemot Rabbah 9:12), who said that the warning preceded for twenty-four days before the plague came, and the plague was active among them for seven days — but according to the one who says that the warning was for seven days and the plague was active among them for twenty-four days, those would be the seven days of warning, and consequently the remainder of the month was when the plague was active among them. Yet it is difficult for his view from the plague of darkness, and perhaps that one was an exception to the general rule, and it is possible that the plague of the Nile too was an exception, and the one who says the plague was active for twenty-four days would concede that the Nile plague did not last long, and both of them intend the same meaning in the verse's statement that it said ״שִׁבְעַת יָמִים אַחֲרֵי הַכּוֹת״ — that it was not smitten for more than seven days, like the rule of the plague of darkness, which was not longer than seven. And I am of the opinion that even though there was a limit for the plague, it would have withdrawn if Moses had prayed before that time."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The verse citation in the commentary text reads simply ויאמר ה׳ with no chapter address; the Hebrew uses ה׳ as a reverent abbreviation, rendered here as HaShem per the voice rules."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:45.174769037Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}